Receive windows that grow when, and as far as, quic-go's do.

quic-go auto-tunes a receive window by epochs (maybeAdjustWindowSize,
vendor/quic-go/flow_controller_base.go:55-75): an epoch begins with the first stream data and again
after every adjustment; when a window update is written and more than half the window has been read
in the epoch, in less than four times that fraction of the smoothed RTT, the window doubles up to
its ceiling. A stream whose window grew raises the connection's to one and a half times its own
(EnsureMinimumWindowSize, vendor/quic-go/flow_controller_connection.go:150-165). And the update
itself is due once what is left of the advertised window has fallen to three quarters of it
(hasWindowUpdate, :35-39).

Upstream ngtcp2 grows a window when two updates come within two RTTs of each other, and sends an
update only once MORE than a quarter has been read. This patch puts quic-go's rules in both places,
with max_window and max_stream_window as quic-go's MaxConnectionReceiveWindow and
MaxStreamReceiveWindow.

For a client that does not parrot Chrome the ceilings are hysteria's defaults, 8 and 20 MB, the
same as the windows it starts with (vendor/hysteria/core/client/config.go:51-53, :61-63), so
nothing grows, as nothing grows in the reference. A client parroting Chrome starts at Chrome's 6 and
15 MB (vendor/quic-go/config.go:109-125) under the same ceilings, and there the windows do grow:
the stream's once to 8 MB, the connection's to 20 MB.

